{
    "title": "onWater Fish - Fishing Spots",
    "description": "Stop Guessing and Start Fishing With Fishing Access For All\r\nFrom knowing what species to target, to where and when, onWater Fish is your personal guide to the water, providing real-time fishing data and robust planning tools for a more self-reliant day on the water.\r\nonWater Fish has an extensive database of fishing spots, including over 100,000 public access points, boat ramps, and even fly and tackle shops, across more than 224,000 lakes and 201,000 rivers. This makes it easier than ever to find the perfect spot to fish.\r\nonWater Fish also features an industry-first fish species map layer, allowing you to visually explore the habitats of over 100 different fish. This valuable information helps you tailor your approach and increase your chances of success when targeting specific species.\r\nonWater Fish provides crucial weather forecasts and river flow conditions to plan your fishing trip. With access to flow stations and detailed river cards, you can gain valuable insights into the current conditions and make informed decisions about your fishing trips.\r\nFly fishing and conventional anglers will both find useful fishing information with access to detailed fishing maps and vital information for the fish in each river and lake, making it easier than ever to fish new waters.\r\nonWater Fish is more than just a fishing map or fishing app. It's a one-stop shop for all your fishing needs, offering valuable tools and information to help you fish and make the most of your time on the water. Download onWater Fish today, discover new fishing spots, and experience the thrill of catching your next fish.\r\nFish smarter with real-time insights\r\nExperience the freedom of fishing with the most comprehensive e-scouting tool in your pocket. \r\nConditions Monitoring: Keep an eye on up to two free favorite rivers and lakes with My Waters. Your personal dashboard for current and forecast USGS Streamflows so you can fish under ideal conditions.\r\nPublic Land Boundaries: Fish public land along all of the nation's waterways, so you can find new fishing access spots.  \r\n\r\n\r\nFishing regulations: Stay informed about local fishing regulations and restrictions directly within the app. onWater Fish provides easy access to this core information, helping you fish responsibly, regardless of the species you're targeting.\r\nFishing Journal: Keep your personal fishing journal on your phone, where you can record the days conditions, your locations, fish caught, and more.  \r\nFish like a local, wherever you go\r\nonWater Fish offers a subscription that unlocks additional functionalities, further enhancing your fishing experience. \r\nReal-time water conditions: Keep a detailed eye on the conditions for an unlimited # of waters, making sure you always know where the best fishing is going to be. \r\nAdvanced distance measuring: Measure floats with onWaters powerful distance measuring tool, so you always know exactly how far you have to go.  \r\nOffline maps: Take your fishing information with you, even in remote areas with limited internet access. Download detailed maps for offline use and avoid getting lost on your next fishing trip on unfamiliar waters.\r\nPrivate Property Boundaries: Know who owns the land, so you can avoid landowner conflicts and fish legally.  \r\n3d Maps: See where you will be fishing, before you go.  \r\nFish Species Layer: Target over 100 fish species with our intuitive map layer, perfect for diversifying your fishing experience based on different bodies of water.\r\nExperience the power of streamlined research and real-time data. onWater Fish allows you to plan and adapt your fishing trips with ease.\r\nWhether conditions shift or you're looking to fish the best spots based on current flows, we enable you to make informed decisions on the fly, so you can fish more efficiently.",
